ave problems if we would  close the border between  turkey and the islamic state because  every day some 100 or 200 fresh  fighters from western countries or from  other parts of the world  are crossing these borders i've been  crossing this border too  not as a fighter but as an observer they  would have big problems if they wouldn't  get  fresh fighters and they can only fight  and they can  only survive because they have made a  cooperation  with those groups of the iraqi and the  syrian population which are excluded  from the political process  i'm talking about the sunnis for example  in iraq  the sunnis have been excluded after the  american invasion in 2003  completely and therefore they are  tolerating  is and if it would be if you would  succeed in creating a national  reconciliation  in iraq and to make peace  in iraq and if we would be successful  to have a national reconciliation also  in syria  between the regime and some of the  rebels  some parts of the population and if you  would have peace  in syria this would have be a big  problem because  they would be finished like a fish  without water guerrillas need  part of the population supporting them  and  we should do everything to get this  national reconciliation in iraq and this  year and this would be a strategy  which would be very dangerous what about  the  70 000 troops on the ground that our  prime minister has spoken  so much about of late how intimidating  how  threatening uh what might they be able  to bring  to threaten islamic state  you are talking about which troops the  troops of  assad or no no no so the so the british  government as far as our prime minister  is concerned when he was speaking to the  house of commons  last week he talked about 70  000 uh troops pro-syrian  army troops who would be able to be  brought  together not necessarily under one  banner but at the present  they are rebels in varying parts of the  country  they could be brought together to fight  islamic state  