erners over the last  18 months two years so i wonder about  your emotions  as as you went to spend time with them  and also what did you see while you were  there  i saw many things i had a list and i  would say 70  of the things i wanted to see i could  see and  i saw horrible things i saw a  kurdish hostage and i spoke to him and  this  these are moments i will never forget  how helpless this man  was when i came back i tried to do  something for him but it was not  possible  i had the i tried to have the  opportunity to speak to john kentley  i they gave me the opportunity to speak  to him but they said  they would film it and i said i cannot  appear in a propaganda film of  of iis of isis but they were ready to  to bring me together with john candley  and they said  they he had prepared a letter for his  family and the letter for  david cameron i tried to contact  your government when i came back but  your government  refused to do anything and told me that  i  could step out of this question i think  it's a pity because  they were ready to give freedom to  john cantley at a  not for much money they they asked the  release of a  not very important uh woman  so there was a possibility but i was  told  not to to  stay in this problem and  for example i spoke to a judge i have  been  on many places difficult to tell the  whole story of 10 days  but i spoke to a judge about the  executions and amputations  and i said are there new amputations  within the next days or execution he  said no  because we have done some amputations  and now we don't need  anymore we need don't need them anymore  because  the population is doing what we want  them to do  and at this moment when this judge told  me no  you cannot see amputation the execution  i didn't want to see them  i just wanted to know what was happening  one of our is fighters who was always  with us he told me oh  if you would like to take a film about  amputations or execution i can't do that  for you  our prisons